WEBVTT

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:10.451
Support Admin Watch on
kissasia.cam or kisskh.org

00:15.640 --> 00:17.058
I wanna make a toast

00:17.392 --> 00:20.061
to my goofball son, Chrisper.

00:20.395 --> 00:22.272
You've had some hard times...

00:23.148 --> 00:25.025
but you came out the other side
a better man.

00:25.108 --> 00:26.109
Yeah.

00:26.693 --> 00:27.986
And lucky for us,

00:28.069 --> 00:30.822
you realized
that this gorgeous little lady here

00:31.364 --> 00:33.700
is about the best thing
that ever happened to you.

00:33.783 --> 00:34.909
Hear fucking hear!

00:34.993 --> 00:35.994
-Yeah.
-Here, then.

00:36.077 --> 00:37.996
Such wise words, August.

00:39.205 --> 00:40.206
Yep.

00:40.290 --> 00:41.791
You can ask. We'll go with you.

00:41.875 --> 00:43.334
I'm nervous.

00:43.418 --> 00:44.919
-Please.
-Please, please, please, please.

00:45.003 --> 00:46.379
-Come on, let's go.
-Boy.

00:46.463 --> 00:48.381
-Come on, come on. Go.
-So uncool.

00:49.007 --> 00:50.050
Mr. Blue Dragon,

00:50.133 --> 00:51.843
can we get a photo with all you guys?

00:51.926 --> 00:53.470
Absolutely, kids. Gather around.

00:53.553 --> 00:55.597
Blue Dragon loves taking selfies.

00:55.680 --> 00:56.973
Except he's terrible at it.

00:57.057 --> 00:58.558
If you want pictures of your foreheads,

00:58.641 --> 01:00.435
-let him take it.
-Can you believe that?

01:00.518 --> 01:02.270
That's my own son talking to me like that.

01:02.353 --> 01:03.897
You're giving him way too much respect.

01:03.980 --> 01:05.272
Look, it's a horrible photo.

01:05.355 --> 01:06.733
Can you put me in the picture?

01:06.816 --> 01:08.860
-Yeah, that's a little much.
-Emilia, can you save the day?

01:08.943 --> 01:10.153
All right, all right. I'll take it.

01:11.488 --> 01:12.989
She's a professional selfie person.

01:13.073 --> 01:15.033
All right, get in here. Get in here.

01:15.283 --> 01:17.952
-Here we go.
-All right. You ready?

01:19.329 --> 01:20.705
Everybody say, "Top Trio."

01:20.789 --> 01:21.956
-Top Trio!
-Top Trio!

03:28.583 --> 03:30.668
You sure this is our best option?

03:30.752 --> 03:32.837
ARGUS doesn't know
Vigilante's secret identity,

03:32.879 --> 03:35.006
so if we connect from here,
they won't find it.

03:35.089 --> 03:36.382
Hey, just so you guys know,

03:36.466 --> 03:38.885
my mom can be a total be-atch.

03:38.968 --> 03:40.261
Is she going to rat us out?

03:40.345 --> 03:42.889
-No.
-Well, then we don't have another choice.

03:42.972 --> 03:44.641
Are you sure you wanna do this?

03:44.724 --> 03:46.184
You can have your whole career back

03:46.267 --> 03:48.478
if you just turn that silver container
into ARGUS.

03:48.561 --> 03:51.064
All you've talked about for months
is getting your job back.

03:51.147 --> 03:53.483
Then we better do it
before I change my mind.

03:56.110 --> 03:57.153
John, are you in?

03:58.112 --> 03:59.113
No, I'm not in.

03:59.197 --> 04:01.950
I'm just incredibly susceptible
to peer pressure.

04:11.668 --> 04:13.586
-Adrian!
-Hi, Mom.

04:14.003 --> 04:16.464
We're going to my secret room.
You're not allowed to follow.

04:16.547 --> 04:19.384
Hi, Mrs. Chase. I'm Lee, Adrian's friend.

04:19.466 --> 04:20.885
His friend?

04:21.427 --> 04:24.639
Adrian doesn't bring his friends around
very often.

04:24.722 --> 04:26.808
Not since the D&D group broke up.

04:27.809 --> 04:29.394
He didn't have enough players,

04:29.477 --> 04:32.021
so I became a 40th level cutpurse.

04:32.105 --> 04:33.439
Jesus, Mom,

04:33.523 --> 04:35.316
what part of
"You're not allowed to follow,"

04:35.400 --> 04:36.401
don't you understand?

04:36.484 --> 04:38.069
I'm sorry, Adrian. I'm so sorry.

04:38.152 --> 04:40.863
If you're sorry, why are you still coming?
Jesus, fuck.

04:40.947 --> 04:42.407
Anyone else here have a mom

04:42.490 --> 04:44.701
who's a fucking tick on your dick
all the time?

04:45.784 --> 04:47.120
You must be John.

04:47.829 --> 04:49.330
-Jesus!
-You're not that dorky.

04:51.332 --> 04:52.709
And don't tell me.

04:53.209 --> 04:54.961
This is Hardcore?

04:55.044 --> 04:57.880
-Shut up, Mom!
-Harcourt, not Hardcore.

04:57.964 --> 04:59.424
I thought it was Har--

04:59.507 --> 05:00.717
You're not alone, but no.

05:00.800 --> 05:02.385
Mom, we're going into my secret room now,

05:02.468 --> 05:04.137
so do you mind? Scoot.

05:04.220 --> 05:06.055
Of course. Of course. I'm sorry.

05:06.556 --> 05:09.392
And I am so sorry if Adrian hurt you.

05:09.475 --> 05:10.727
-Mom, shut up!
-Excuse me?

05:10.810 --> 05:12.687
I was just so excited
that he had a girlfriend.

05:12.770 --> 05:14.772
-Mom, shut up! Shut up.
-Girlfriend?

05:14.856 --> 05:17.191
I don't think that being too slutty

05:17.275 --> 05:18.776
-is any reason to break up.
-Mom, stop!

05:18.860 --> 05:20.153
Mom, would you please fuck off?

05:20.236 --> 05:21.487
-Go. Mom!
-I told Adrian...

05:21.571 --> 05:23.197
-Stop!
-...it's a new era.

05:23.281 --> 05:25.116
People have the pornography
on their phone now.

05:25.199 --> 05:26.576
Please, fuck off!

05:26.659 --> 05:28.911
-They can't help but be slutty.
-Just zip it.

05:28.995 --> 05:30.496
It's up to a mature man

05:30.580 --> 05:32.623
-to teach his partner...
-Oh my God.

05:32.707 --> 05:35.752
...about how making love
can be a way to connect.

05:35.835 --> 05:36.836
-Oh my God.
-Yeah.

05:36.919 --> 05:38.796
You're hurting my brain. Stop!

05:38.880 --> 05:40.298
Stop!

05:40.381 --> 05:41.382
I'm sorry.

05:42.133 --> 05:44.469
I guess these lovers' quarrels
are none of my beeswax.

05:45.178 --> 05:47.263
I'll see you all when you come upstairs.

05:47.972 --> 05:49.474
I'll make sammiches!

05:53.644 --> 05:54.645
She's great.

05:56.147 --> 05:58.524
Yeah, that was so weird. She has dementia.

05:58.608 --> 06:00.985
I think she was confusing you
with my other girlfriend.

06:01.069 --> 06:02.236
Weird. Yeah.

06:02.320 --> 06:04.280
Also, sometimes I have to say stuff

06:04.364 --> 06:06.407
to hide that I'm out
doing superhero stuff.

06:06.491 --> 06:07.867
Yeah, like I'm slutty?

06:08.451 --> 06:10.244
Yeah, I have to base it in some truth.

06:19.045 --> 06:20.254
Wow.

06:20.338 --> 06:22.131
Holy hell.

06:22.632 --> 06:24.926
What in the fuck is this?

06:25.009 --> 06:27.053
You know,
if I bust up a drug ring or whatever,

06:27.136 --> 06:28.721
I just take everything and I put it here.

06:28.805 --> 06:30.640
-Why?
-Because if I give it to the cops,

06:30.723 --> 06:33.101
there's a good chance they're corrupt
and they could steal it.

06:33.183 --> 06:34.268
Or worse, use it themselves.

06:34.352 --> 06:37.230
Dude, there has to be,
like, millions of dollars here.

06:37.313 --> 06:40.108
Adrian, just last week
you told me you were broke

06:40.191 --> 06:42.151
and asked me to pay for your breakfast.

06:42.235 --> 06:44.654
Well, I'm not gonna use this, man. No way.

06:44.737 --> 06:46.322
It's blood money, you crazy?

06:50.576 --> 06:52.578
Yeah, man,
you don't want to deal with blood money,

06:52.662 --> 06:54.831
and that shit goes to the grave with you.
Trust me.

06:54.914 --> 06:57.166
Hey, what do you guys think
the chances are

06:57.250 --> 06:58.709
I'll meet another me in there?

06:59.585 --> 07:01.629
Prob-- Probably not too likely.

07:01.712 --> 07:04.507
But-- But... we should try
to avoid shit like that

07:04.590 --> 07:06.717
just in case we cause
a dimensional disturbance

07:06.801 --> 07:09.345
-and explode or something.
-It might be worth it, though.

07:10.721 --> 07:11.931
How about this?

07:12.014 --> 07:13.099
That should work.

07:13.182 --> 07:15.476
Okay, but just be careful.
That's my Beanie Baby collection.

07:15.560 --> 07:17.520
I'm pretty sure the market
is about to bounce back

07:17.603 --> 07:19.063
and they're gonna be worth a shitload.

07:19.605 --> 07:21.482
What's with all the ostriches?

07:21.566 --> 07:23.651
Stretch? He's the cutest of them all.

07:23.734 --> 07:26.028
Okay, I think you do this.

07:30.616 --> 07:33.369
Okay, everybody move back a little.

07:33.453 --> 07:34.871
Move back? How far back?

07:34.954 --> 07:36.622
Just go all the way to the wall.

07:37.415 --> 07:38.416
God damn it.

07:39.250 --> 07:40.293
This is fucked.

07:40.835 --> 07:43.254
We are fucked, man. We are insane.

08:02.190 --> 08:04.233
Is this what it's supposed to do?

08:19.624 --> 08:21.082
What the fuck!

08:21.167 --> 08:23.669
I have fucking cocaine all over me!

08:24.462 --> 08:25.421
Fuck, Adrian!

08:25.922 --> 08:28.382
Why can't you fucking
flush your drugs down the toilet

08:28.466 --> 08:29.509
like a normal person?

08:29.592 --> 08:31.886
Because of the alligators
in the sewer system,

08:31.969 --> 08:33.513
you callous piece of shit.

08:33.596 --> 08:35.222
-What?
-Oh my God.

08:35.306 --> 08:37.808
As if the addiction epidemic
facing the country isn't bad enough,

08:37.892 --> 08:40.602
he also wants the alligators in the sewers
to be junkies.

08:40.686 --> 08:41.895
You're a moron.

08:41.979 --> 08:44.607
What the fuck does that have to do
with alligators?

08:44.690 --> 08:45.816
Speaking of which,

08:45.900 --> 08:47.860
does anyone want to quiz me
on alligator facts?

08:47.944 --> 08:49.028
-No!
-No!

08:49.111 --> 08:50.112
That seemed rehearsed.

08:50.196 --> 08:51.531
This is unbelievable.

08:51.614 --> 08:53.449
Okay, how about
I just spit out alligator facts

08:53.533 --> 08:54.617
until there's one you know,

08:54.700 --> 08:56.869
-and then whoever knows it takes over?
-No, Adrian.

08:56.953 --> 08:57.954
Stop it. Come on.

08:58.037 --> 09:00.248
How could Chris not tell us
about any of this?

09:00.331 --> 09:01.958
He said it was like me being Methodist.

09:02.416 --> 09:03.876
It was so normal to him.

09:03.960 --> 09:06.254
He grew up with it,
so he didn't think twice about it.

09:06.337 --> 09:08.923
-Alligators have four stomachs.
-That's cows.

09:11.634 --> 09:13.636
Jesus fucking Christ.

09:14.512 --> 09:15.680
Hi.

09:15.763 --> 09:17.265
Don't wave at it.

09:17.348 --> 09:18.975
Why? I'm being friendly.

09:19.058 --> 09:20.851
You don't know
what waving means to that thing.

09:20.935 --> 09:22.478
The peace sign means "fuck you"
in England

09:22.562 --> 09:24.063
and we speak the same fucking language.

09:24.146 --> 09:26.357
It means "up yours," not "fuck you."

09:26.440 --> 09:28.442
Okay. Well, I'll be sure
in pointing out the nuances

09:28.526 --> 09:29.860
to the Xenomorph over there

09:29.944 --> 09:31.153
after he rips your head off

09:31.237 --> 09:33.114
for telling him
his favorite son should die

09:33.197 --> 09:34.824
'cause that's what fucking waving means.

09:34.907 --> 09:36.033
What are you fucking doing?

09:36.117 --> 09:37.868
Waving means your favorite son should die?

09:37.952 --> 09:38.953
-No.
-No.

09:39.036 --> 09:40.121
That's such a simple gesture

09:40.204 --> 09:42.498
to mean something so complicated
that you'll hardly ever say.

09:42.582 --> 09:43.915
How do we know where Chris went?

09:44.000 --> 09:46.586
He said there was a lock on the door
like the one back there

09:46.669 --> 09:47.962
and a rack of Peacemaker helmets.

09:48.004 --> 09:49.463
We just need to look for that.

09:59.265 --> 10:00.349
-Hey, Chief.
-Yeah?

10:00.433 --> 10:02.184
In addition to losing Peacemaker,

10:02.268 --> 10:05.563
Economos and Emilia Harcourt are both MIA.

10:06.230 --> 10:07.607
Jesus Christ.

10:08.858 --> 10:10.651
Has Judomaster made any contact?

10:11.319 --> 10:12.945
No. Can't find him either.

10:13.487 --> 10:14.614
Fuck me, man!

10:15.323 --> 10:16.866
We need to find Peacemaker.

10:16.949 --> 10:18.951
I don't think you understand
how important this is

10:19.035 --> 10:20.995
to the United States, to the world.

10:21.871 --> 10:24.040
Well, I don't know the protocol.

10:24.123 --> 10:27.209
-Should we put out an APB on--
-Just stop. Just stop.

10:27.710 --> 10:28.794
Don't do anything.

10:30.171 --> 10:31.589
Just give me a second to think.

10:44.602 --> 10:45.853
You're kidding me, right?

10:47.146 --> 10:48.147
Alone.

10:49.065 --> 10:51.442
-Please.
-Okay.

10:52.610 --> 10:53.611
Cool.

10:54.570 --> 10:55.696
Fucking idiots.

11:04.121 --> 11:06.040
Jessica, have the jet prepped

11:06.123 --> 11:08.584
to leave for St. Roch, Louisiana
in a half hour.

11:08.668 --> 11:11.128
I want you
to call the warden of Belle Reve Prison.

11:11.212 --> 11:13.005
You tell him
I'm coming to meet a prisoner.

11:16.050 --> 11:17.093
Guys.

11:17.385 --> 11:18.761
Guys, come over here.

11:19.512 --> 11:21.222
Yo, can you hear me? Hey!

11:23.849 --> 11:24.892
Wow.

11:25.726 --> 11:28.187
I guess that rules out this being
a figment of Chris's imagination.

11:28.270 --> 11:29.355
Yeah.

11:32.108 --> 11:33.859
Hey, John, can you hack this lock?

11:34.527 --> 11:35.820
Not without all my shit.

11:36.612 --> 11:37.613
Two-six-one-zero-one-one.

11:37.697 --> 11:39.073
What?

11:39.156 --> 11:41.325
That's Chris's dad's code.
I'm guessing it's the same.

11:42.368 --> 11:43.369
Say it again.

11:43.452 --> 11:46.247
Two-six-one-zero-one-one.

12:04.181 --> 12:06.267
No wonder Chris likes it here.

12:07.351 --> 12:09.770
Top of the town.

12:10.646 --> 12:12.148
Nice digs.

12:12.857 --> 12:15.151
Reverse Peacemaker's rolling in it.

12:15.234 --> 12:16.944
How the heck are we supposed to find him?

12:17.027 --> 12:19.864
I don't know. Maybe just find some place
to camp out here until he's back.

12:19.947 --> 12:22.491
Don't you think I should go and see
if there's another me somewhere?

12:22.575 --> 12:23.576
Why would you do that?

12:23.659 --> 12:25.786
Because maybe I'm best friends
with Peacemaker here, too.

12:25.870 --> 12:28.038
That's probably a constant
throughout the multiverse.

12:28.122 --> 12:30.791
And I bet Vigilante 2 is a rad guy
who could help us out.

12:30.875 --> 12:33.711
I wouldn't count on that.
Chris's doppelganger tried to kill him.

12:34.295 --> 12:35.337
I know.

12:35.379 --> 12:37.298
I helped him incinerate his corpse.

12:43.804 --> 12:44.930
Fucking creepy.

12:45.806 --> 12:46.807
This is fucked up.

12:46.891 --> 12:48.893
This whole fucking thing
is really fucking wrong, Ads.

12:48.976 --> 12:50.936
There's no way Chris should be here.

12:51.020 --> 12:52.980
Like, maybe just trust
in the wisdom of the universe

12:53.063 --> 12:54.064
just a little bit.

12:54.148 --> 12:55.858
It put us in a completely
different dimension--

12:55.941 --> 12:56.942
Emilia?

13:00.571 --> 13:02.156
Sorry, I just took a shit in there.

13:03.115 --> 13:04.366
It's...

13:05.201 --> 13:06.202
rancid.

13:06.994 --> 13:08.454
So, what's up? How's it going?

13:09.747 --> 13:12.166
Good. Good. I thought you were with Chris.

13:12.583 --> 13:14.752
I was. I was. But, you know...

13:15.294 --> 13:16.712
He said he was heading to ARGUS.

13:16.754 --> 13:18.422
I figured you two just would be together.

13:20.132 --> 13:22.134
No. No, no, no.

13:22.218 --> 13:24.929
He dropped me off here so that I could...

13:25.805 --> 13:26.847
pick up...

13:28.516 --> 13:31.060
this thing... for him.

13:31.143 --> 13:32.853
Why would he want you to get that?

13:32.937 --> 13:33.938
Right?

13:35.439 --> 13:39.944
Yeah, I mean, he said, you know,
take this thing and...

13:40.027 --> 13:42.029
put it on your desk, so...

13:42.947 --> 13:44.281
You know, you...

13:45.407 --> 13:46.826
you shake it and then snow comes.

13:47.493 --> 13:49.245
That's what most snow globes do.

13:49.912 --> 13:50.955
Right?

13:51.872 --> 13:53.707
Yeah, why was he so weird about it?

13:54.458 --> 13:56.377
Our mother gave him that on her deathbed.

13:57.044 --> 13:58.128
So, I'm just

13:58.212 --> 14:01.465
kind of surprised he's giving it to you.

14:02.049 --> 14:03.133
Me too.

14:04.885 --> 14:05.970
Yeah.

14:06.220 --> 14:07.221
Well...

14:08.514 --> 14:10.850
I guess I should get going back to work.

14:10.933 --> 14:12.768
I'm-- I'm heading to ARGUS
if you want a ride.

14:14.645 --> 14:15.688
Oh.

14:16.438 --> 14:17.481
I...

14:21.694 --> 14:23.529
Okay, sure. Why not?

14:24.196 --> 14:25.197
You know, it's wild.

14:25.281 --> 14:26.699
I've never seen you wear black before.

14:27.199 --> 14:28.200
-No?
-No.

14:28.784 --> 14:30.744
-Or pants.
-Pants?

14:30.828 --> 14:32.538
What, I'm always in my fucking underwear?

14:33.497 --> 14:35.290
You're just as weird as your boyfriend is.

14:35.665 --> 14:37.585
You got white stuff in your hair,
by the way.

14:37.668 --> 14:38.919
Thanks for pointing that out.

14:39.003 --> 14:40.254
What'd she do that for?

14:40.337 --> 14:42.381
Maybe she's hoping
he'll lead her straight to Chris.

14:42.923 --> 14:43.924
Who was that?

14:44.008 --> 14:46.343
That was Chris's dead brother, Keith.

14:47.928 --> 14:50.139
Oh, no. Are you fucking kidding me?

14:50.222 --> 14:51.223
No.

14:53.809 --> 14:55.060
Oh my God.

14:56.562 --> 14:57.563
Yo.

14:57.730 --> 14:59.732
Oh my God. Don't throw up, man.

14:59.815 --> 15:01.275
Why is that making you throw up?

15:01.358 --> 15:02.359
It's too fucking weird.

15:02.443 --> 15:04.278
Being weird doesn't make
normal people throw up.

15:04.361 --> 15:06.864
-I've never even heard of that.
-It happens all the time.

15:06.947 --> 15:08.741
I thought it was neat
to meet someone dead.

15:08.824 --> 15:10.367
Also, not normal.

15:10.451 --> 15:11.869
We-- We should turn back.

15:11.952 --> 15:13.829
Go back and forget this shit.

15:13.913 --> 15:15.331
And just leave Harcourt here, too?

15:15.414 --> 15:17.124
-Get the fuck out of here.
-Right.

15:17.207 --> 15:19.335
What I think we need to do
is divide and conquer.

15:19.418 --> 15:20.461
-No.
-I should go

15:20.544 --> 15:21.962
-and find my other self...
-No!

15:22.004 --> 15:23.756
...and question him about Peacemaker.
Why no?

15:23.839 --> 15:25.966
Adrian,
yesterday you were crying in my arms

15:26.050 --> 15:27.885
-because Chris left us.
-No, I wasn't.

15:27.968 --> 15:28.969
Okay.

15:29.053 --> 15:31.138
I wasn't crying. That wasn't crying, Ads.

15:31.221 --> 15:33.015
I gave you a hug to comfort you.

15:33.098 --> 15:34.850
You were crying like a little baby!

15:34.934 --> 15:36.226
All right, whatever the case,

15:36.310 --> 15:38.604
it seems like now
you don't even care about Chris.

15:38.687 --> 15:40.272
You just want to meet your other self.

15:42.024 --> 15:43.651
Maybe we just stay here forever.

15:44.485 --> 15:46.570
Wow, that's a sharp left turn.

15:46.654 --> 15:48.530
I mean, everything I like is here.

15:48.614 --> 15:51.867
Eagly, Peacemaker, you guys, another me.

15:51.951 --> 15:54.370
I mean, if they have manta rays and crows,
I'm good to go.

15:54.453 --> 15:56.830
We are going back after we get Chris,

15:56.914 --> 15:58.832
-and now Harcourt.
-Okay, well,

15:58.915 --> 16:00.834
then I need to go find myself
and question him.

16:00.918 --> 16:02.544
No, Adrian, come on, man.

16:02.628 --> 16:04.213
I'll be right back. I won't be long.

16:09.343 --> 16:10.594
Come the fuck on.

16:51.093 --> 16:52.177
You like Helloween?

16:53.095 --> 16:54.972
-Helloween?
-Yeah.

16:55.055 --> 16:56.807
They say it's between them
and the Beatles.

16:57.433 --> 16:58.434
For what?

16:59.059 --> 17:00.436
Greatest rock band ever.

17:00.519 --> 17:02.396
I mean, I know. It's a stupid argument.

17:02.479 --> 17:03.564
It's subjective.

17:03.647 --> 17:06.775
But to me... Helloween, I mean,
they might have all the hits,

17:06.858 --> 17:09.737
but... they didn't revolutionize
rock and roll

17:09.819 --> 17:12.321
the way that Mick, Paul, George,
and Ringo did.

17:12.906 --> 17:14.532
-Mick?
-Jagger?

17:15.492 --> 17:16.785
Lead singer of the Beatles?

17:18.954 --> 17:20.455
-Right. Yeah.
-Yeah.

17:21.290 --> 17:22.875
-Sorry.
-It's...

17:23.416 --> 17:25.461
God, Chris is spot-on about you.

17:26.170 --> 17:27.546
You spent all those years in books.

17:27.628 --> 17:30.049
You don't know the first thing
about the most basic

17:30.132 --> 17:31.425
of pop culture trivia.

17:32.551 --> 17:33.594
I mean, I love it.

17:33.677 --> 17:37.139
'Cause me and Chris, God,
we need you to class us up.

17:37.222 --> 17:38.223
Really.

17:39.058 --> 17:40.059
Yep.

17:41.310 --> 17:44.229
Yeah, I've spent my whole life in books.

17:52.613 --> 17:54.656
Hey, Keith wanted me to go down to ARGUS

17:54.740 --> 17:56.742
to fill out some paperwork
on the Kaiju fight.

17:57.659 --> 18:00.079
You want me to wait?
You want me to meet you down there?

18:00.162 --> 18:02.081
No, no worries. You go ahead.

18:02.164 --> 18:03.207
I'll meet you there.

18:03.290 --> 18:05.042
I've got some stuff to take care of here.

18:54.383 --> 18:55.676
Whoa, whoa, girl!

18:55.759 --> 18:57.302
Eva! Eva!

18:57.386 --> 18:59.096
Heel! Heel!

18:59.179 --> 19:01.431
I'm sorry, miss.
Eva detects an illicit substance.

19:01.515 --> 19:03.475
I'm gonna need you to hold right there.

19:05.144 --> 19:06.562
Fucking Adrian.

19:06.645 --> 19:07.855
Hey, guys,

19:07.938 --> 19:09.565
I'm sure there's just been
a misunderstanding here.

19:09.648 --> 19:10.858
I'm sure, sir.

19:10.941 --> 19:13.485
But I'm gonna need you
to come with me, miss.

19:13.569 --> 19:14.653
I-- I'm sorry.

19:20.033 --> 19:21.493
I'm so sorry, Miss Harcourt.

19:26.206 --> 19:27.749
Don't worry, we'll get you out of this.

19:31.420 --> 19:33.839
-I'll get this back to you.
-Shove it up your ass.

19:35.048 --> 19:36.133
Right this way, miss.

19:50.647 --> 19:54.443
Oh my gosh!
My house looks almost exactly the same.

19:54.526 --> 19:57.029
So cool.

20:02.743 --> 20:03.744
What?

20:04.036 --> 20:05.662
Who are you guys?

20:09.833 --> 20:12.252
You're a chipmunk in my world.

20:19.468 --> 20:20.510
What--

20:21.970 --> 20:23.347
What is this?

20:23.430 --> 20:26.808
Did I make you?
Supposed to be a snake, not a dragon.

20:29.645 --> 20:32.606
What? But there's supposed to be three!
Why are there six?

20:32.689 --> 20:35.108
What do six cats have to talk about?

20:37.736 --> 20:39.947
Oh my God, what the fuck is this?

20:41.240 --> 20:43.200
They spell it just a little differently.

20:43.283 --> 20:44.618
Oh my God, that's amazing.

20:45.285 --> 20:46.745
I'm keeping this shit.

20:52.209 --> 20:54.461
My Dad's not gay here.

21:15.691 --> 21:16.692
No way.

21:21.154 --> 21:22.572
Are you kidding me?

21:27.786 --> 21:28.787
Yes.

21:29.079 --> 21:30.163
Unbelievable.

21:38.380 --> 21:39.381
Hello?

21:40.132 --> 21:41.133
What the fuck?

21:43.010 --> 21:44.803
Who are you, and why are you here?

21:44.886 --> 21:47.222
Dude, hold on. Hold on, hold on, dude.
Dude.

21:48.974 --> 21:50.225
It's me.

21:50.309 --> 21:52.185
I'm you from another dimension.

21:52.269 --> 21:54.563
My keys worked to get in here.

21:57.649 --> 21:59.318
Are you fucking kidding me?

21:59.401 --> 22:01.403
-No!
-Holy shit!

22:01.486 --> 22:03.155
-Hey!
-We--

22:03.238 --> 22:04.489
We Spider-Man meme'd!

22:05.574 --> 22:07.409
Hey! Hey! Hey!

22:07.492 --> 22:08.577
-Hey!
-Hey!

22:10.662 --> 22:13.206
So, we're just supposed to wait here
until they get back?

22:13.623 --> 22:15.000
What else are we gonna do?

22:16.960 --> 22:19.796
We should probably wait back in our world,
don't you think?

22:19.880 --> 22:21.923
I mean, what if the White Dragon shows up?

22:22.007 --> 22:24.134
Dude, why did you even come?

22:29.681 --> 22:30.932
Eagly!

22:34.061 --> 22:36.021
Dude, what are you doing?

22:36.605 --> 22:37.814
Creating a mess.

22:39.024 --> 22:40.025
Boy.

22:40.525 --> 22:41.610
God.

22:45.572 --> 22:47.282
Yo, we gotta clean this up.

22:47.366 --> 22:50.494
We're traveling between dimensions
to clean up Eagly's bullshit?

22:51.745 --> 22:54.456
-Fuck, Jesus.
-Okay, all right.

23:40.627 --> 23:43.505
General Flag. What an unexpected delight.

23:44.172 --> 23:45.173
Lex.

23:45.257 --> 23:46.258
Last time I saw you,

23:46.341 --> 23:48.718
you were denying metahumans were a threat.

23:49.386 --> 23:50.804
And now it seems

23:50.887 --> 23:52.431
they're taking over the world.

23:53.432 --> 23:54.474
Sort of, yeah.

23:54.558 --> 23:58.019
You have the Justice Gang and Superman
determining international politics.

23:58.103 --> 24:00.063
Meanwhile,
I'm here in Belle Reve

24:00.147 --> 24:02.691
listening to a bear-sized man
with dragon skin

24:02.774 --> 24:04.943
butt-fucking a glowing twink
with cartoon eyes

24:05.026 --> 24:06.987
in a cell beside me every night.

24:07.779 --> 24:09.531
I did everything I could

24:09.614 --> 24:11.950
to eradicate the metahuman blight,

24:12.033 --> 24:14.619
and now I'm enshrouded in it
for the next...

24:15.245 --> 24:16.371
What did the judge say?

24:17.080 --> 24:19.958
Two hundred and sixty-five years.

24:20.375 --> 24:22.502
What if I can get you
transferred to another prison?

24:22.586 --> 24:23.837
What kind of other prison?

24:23.962 --> 24:24.921
One with no metahumans.

24:25.005 --> 24:27.716
I see you need my help,
and you're here to barter.

24:27.799 --> 24:29.384
Well, if you're willing to start

24:29.468 --> 24:31.052
with an offer of choicer surroundings,

24:31.136 --> 24:33.513
then where you end
will undoubtedly be significantly better.

24:33.597 --> 24:36.016
So, why don't you just start
with your final offer

24:36.099 --> 24:37.934
and not waste either of our times?

24:38.018 --> 24:40.937
You won't be able to outmaneuver me
in negotiations, General.

24:41.021 --> 24:43.482
I don't even know
if you can give me what I need, Lex.

24:43.565 --> 24:45.942
Then, by all means,
what is it you're looking for?

24:46.485 --> 24:47.736
You heard of Peacemaker?

24:47.819 --> 24:49.112
-Meta?
-No.

24:49.196 --> 24:51.114
Just a costumed vigilante.

24:51.198 --> 24:53.950
Then who gives a shit?
Being goofy is no threat.

24:54.576 --> 24:56.828
But he's in possession
of some kind of dimensional portal.

24:57.579 --> 24:59.039
He's able to move it around.

24:59.122 --> 25:01.374
Keeps popping in and out
of the Maridal Radar.

25:03.251 --> 25:04.461
I need to find it.

25:05.003 --> 25:06.046
Why?

25:06.129 --> 25:08.798
For one thing, I don't need another rift
tearing apart half the city.

25:09.841 --> 25:10.884
That hurts.

25:10.967 --> 25:12.677
But I have another idea.

25:12.761 --> 25:15.305
One which could be beneficial
for all of us.

25:17.891 --> 25:20.560
So, if I had a scanner,

25:20.644 --> 25:22.854
say, that could pinpoint
the location of that portal,

25:22.938 --> 25:24.189
that would be of use?

25:25.607 --> 25:26.650
Yes, it would.

25:27.526 --> 25:29.402
Enough to give me my freedom.

25:30.028 --> 25:32.572
Not a fucking chance.
Not gonna happen, Lex.

25:32.906 --> 25:34.157
Then what could I get?

25:34.407 --> 25:37.786
What is the United States government
willing to give me to stop this clown?

25:37.869 --> 25:39.704
An opportunity for redemption.

25:41.831 --> 25:42.832
I'm listening.

25:45.085 --> 25:46.127
Thanks, man.

25:46.211 --> 25:47.963
Hey, thanks.
I appreciate you letting me in.

25:48.046 --> 25:49.089
I know it's not protocol.

25:55.595 --> 25:58.014
-Are they letting me out of here or what?
-What are you doing?

25:58.098 --> 25:59.933
How'd you even get here?
What the fuck is going on?

26:00.016 --> 26:01.685
What are you doing, Chris?

26:01.768 --> 26:03.937
I told you. I wrote the letter.

26:04.020 --> 26:05.438
That letter was bullshit.

26:05.522 --> 26:06.648
It was fucking heartfelt!

26:06.731 --> 26:07.983
Fuck that shit!

26:09.609 --> 26:11.319
I fucking forgave you
for double-crossing me.

26:11.403 --> 26:13.863
I didn't fucking double-cross you, Chris.

26:13.947 --> 26:16.074
-I saved your goddamn life.
-What?

26:16.157 --> 26:19.578
A cyborg had a gun pointed at your head
and was about to take you out.

26:19.661 --> 26:22.330
The only way that I could save you
was to do what I did.

26:22.998 --> 26:24.749
And you should have fucking known that.

26:24.833 --> 26:28.712
You should know that I would never,
ever do something like that to you.

26:29.546 --> 26:31.548
-Sorry.
-And so that hurt my feelings,

26:31.631 --> 26:32.674
to be honest.

26:32.757 --> 26:34.342
You want to talk about feelings?

26:34.426 --> 26:37.220
Jesus, fuck, I said sorry!
How many times do you want me to say it?

26:37.304 --> 26:38.972
At least give me fucking twice.

26:40.015 --> 26:41.057
Okay.

26:42.225 --> 26:43.685
Are they letting me out of here?

26:44.853 --> 26:46.187
You didn't have any drugs on you.

26:46.271 --> 26:48.023
I trust your blood
isn't gonna test positive?

26:48.106 --> 26:49.107
Of course not.

26:49.190 --> 26:51.109
Yeah, so I think so.
Why were you covered in cocaine?

26:51.192 --> 26:54.654
Because Vigilante's a moron
and has Al Capone's vault in his basement.

26:54.738 --> 26:57.407
Never been. Heard about it.
A lot of Beanie Babies?

26:57.741 --> 26:59.576
Not as many as kilos of fentanyl.

26:59.659 --> 27:00.744
Why are you here?

27:00.827 --> 27:02.829
We're all here, Chris.

27:03.455 --> 27:05.081
To get you to come back.

27:05.707 --> 27:08.877
Me, Ads, Adrian, even Economos.

27:11.171 --> 27:14.090
You can't do this, man.
This isn't where you belong.

27:14.174 --> 27:16.051
I tried to talk to you about this
in the park.

27:16.134 --> 27:17.385
In the park,

27:17.469 --> 27:19.971
surrounded by agents
with guns pointed at your head.

27:20.055 --> 27:22.098
That's where you wanted
to have a real heart-to-heart?

27:22.182 --> 27:23.850
Fine! Let's talk about it now.

27:23.933 --> 27:26.102
Why don't you tell me how you feel?

27:26.936 --> 27:29.230
-What?
-About what happened on the boat.

27:29.439 --> 27:31.483
Oh my God.

27:32.192 --> 27:33.318
It's always the boat.

27:33.860 --> 27:36.196
You can't even talk about it.
That's the thing.

27:37.030 --> 27:39.407
And you never even told me
about you and Rick Flag Junior.

27:39.866 --> 27:40.867
I know.

27:41.576 --> 27:43.036
So, what, you guys were a thing?

27:44.537 --> 27:46.581
He was my friend, and he had a girlfriend.

27:46.665 --> 27:50.210
But I guess, yeah, we had a thing,
as mortifying as that is to say.

27:50.919 --> 27:52.045
This whole time, I've been trying

27:52.212 --> 27:54.214
to get close to somebody
whose boyfriend I killed.

27:54.339 --> 27:56.383
-He wasn't my boyfriend.
-Yeah.

27:57.300 --> 27:58.885
I didn't hide it, Chris.

27:58.968 --> 28:02.222
I made my disdain for you
pretty apparent when we first met.

28:02.305 --> 28:03.306
Yeah.

28:03.973 --> 28:05.975
That changed, of course. I...

28:06.601 --> 28:09.020
-I know you don't hate me.
-I know you know I don't.

28:14.651 --> 28:16.027
But I'm in love with you, Emilia.

28:19.030 --> 28:20.198
Yeah, I know.

28:20.490 --> 28:21.658
Yeah, I figured.

28:23.660 --> 28:25.578
You know,
can we just talk about that then, maybe?

28:26.621 --> 28:27.831
Just tell me the truth.

28:29.332 --> 28:30.834
Do you have feelings about me or not?

28:30.917 --> 28:32.877
So, what? So, you're going to stay here

28:32.961 --> 28:35.422
if I don't and come home if I do?

28:35.505 --> 28:37.465
See? You just keep talking around it.

28:37.549 --> 28:40.301
Chris, I'm a fucking nightmare!

28:40.385 --> 28:42.011
I don't care.

28:42.095 --> 28:43.263
I do, okay?

28:43.346 --> 28:46.099
I don't have access to my feelings
like you do.

28:47.392 --> 28:50.687
So-- So, you're right, what you said
on the roof the other night.

28:51.855 --> 28:54.816
What I do is I go and I get in bar fights.

28:54.899 --> 28:57.694
-I know.
-Just so I can fucking feel something.

28:58.236 --> 28:59.446
And I still love you.

29:07.078 --> 29:09.581
Are you coming back or not?

29:10.582 --> 29:12.041
-I can't.
-Yes, you can.

29:12.125 --> 29:13.543
Emilia, my dad...

29:14.878 --> 29:16.004
my brother.

29:16.588 --> 29:17.630
You know, I...

29:17.714 --> 29:18.965
I like the other you, you know?

29:19.048 --> 29:20.425
She's nice. She's not you.

29:20.508 --> 29:22.177
But I can't just run out on these people.

29:27.515 --> 29:28.725
Fucking bullshit.

29:32.645 --> 29:35.064
Blood tested negative for drugs.
She's clear to go.

29:48.912 --> 29:50.205
Did he give you what you need?

29:50.288 --> 29:52.248
-He did.
-And in return?

29:52.874 --> 29:54.834
We're going to transfer him to Van Kull.

29:56.002 --> 29:57.754
-And?
-Not much else.

29:58.880 --> 30:01.132
Other than now
we're partners with Lex Luthor.

30:05.053 --> 30:06.971
Okay, here's one. What's the best Pokémon?

30:07.055 --> 30:08.348
-Infernape!
-Yes!

30:08.431 --> 30:10.475
What's the best thing
to press your face against?

30:10.558 --> 30:11.559
-Shag carpeting.
-Yes!

30:11.643 --> 30:13.394
But what's the worst thing
to softly touch you?

30:13.478 --> 30:14.687
Human skin.

30:15.104 --> 30:16.147
Yes.

30:16.231 --> 30:17.649
What's the coolest thing about a platypus?

30:18.191 --> 30:20.276
Poisonous spike on the back of his ankles!

30:21.152 --> 30:23.196
Are you able to pee
if something's touching your butt?

30:23.279 --> 30:25.573
-No way. I look down upon people who can.
-Right?

30:25.657 --> 30:27.158
Do you ever look up at the clouds,

30:27.242 --> 30:29.285
and you see a face in the clouds
looking down at you,

30:29.369 --> 30:31.329
and you go,
"This isn't a figment of my imagination,

30:31.412 --> 30:32.872
that's a cloud man looking down at me,

30:32.956 --> 30:34.916
and now I have to go inside,
so he can't see me?"

30:34.999 --> 30:37.085
Every day. Is your favorite color teal?

30:37.168 --> 30:39.254
Yes. Is your favorite food Malt-O-Meal?

30:39.379 --> 30:41.422
Yes. Does your hair
look best at 3:00 p.m.?

30:41.506 --> 30:43.007
Yes. Is your best friend Peacemaker?

30:43.091 --> 30:44.092
-Peacemaker?
-Yes.

30:44.175 --> 30:46.094
-I fucking hate that guy.
-What?

30:46.177 --> 30:49.556
I've dedicated my entire life
to tearing down everything he stands for.

30:49.639 --> 30:51.099
You're friends with Peacemaker?

30:51.182 --> 30:54.561
Yes. He's... He's my BFF.
We're two peas in a pod.

30:54.644 --> 30:56.229
Peacemaker?! Christopher Smith?!

30:56.312 --> 30:58.523
-Yeah.
-He's my fucking archenemy.

30:58.606 --> 31:00.275
He's the reason
I joined the Sons of Liberty

31:00.358 --> 31:02.068
-in the first place.
-The what?

31:11.244 --> 31:12.495
Wanna go for a walk?

31:13.288 --> 31:14.289
No way.

31:14.747 --> 31:16.499
Just around the block, John.

31:16.583 --> 31:17.792
Clear our heads.

31:18.293 --> 31:19.586
It's safer than in here.

31:20.086 --> 31:21.254
I'm staying.

31:21.337 --> 31:22.338
Fine.

31:23.006 --> 31:24.090
Suit yourself.

31:28.469 --> 31:29.721
Oh, that's not trash.

32:07.842 --> 32:09.385
Hey, Billy, how's it going?

32:15.975 --> 32:18.311
Miss Harcourt? Miss Harcourt!

32:24.609 --> 32:26.819
You don't notice anything weird here?

32:26.903 --> 32:27.987
No, like what?

32:36.663 --> 32:37.956
She's there!

32:43.711 --> 32:47.090
I haven't seen a single person of color
ever since I've been here.

32:48.341 --> 32:49.342
No way.

32:50.843 --> 32:53.262
One got out! A Black!

32:53.346 --> 32:54.889
What?

33:01.354 --> 33:02.563
Hey!

33:06.192 --> 33:08.486
-Stop her!
-I've got her!

33:08.569 --> 33:10.071
What the fuck?

33:18.329 --> 33:19.372
Fuck me.

33:20.415 --> 33:22.375
This is your perfect world, huh?

33:33.761 --> 33:35.471
No! No! No!

33:37.682 --> 33:39.809
My fucking hand, bro!

33:40.393 --> 33:42.729
-Who the fuck are you?
-I'm John Economos.

33:42.812 --> 33:43.896
I'm from another dimension.

33:43.980 --> 33:45.565
I'm here to get our friend Peacemaker,

33:45.648 --> 33:47.358
who's your son,
but he's not really your son.

33:47.442 --> 33:48.568
I guess he killed your son.

33:48.651 --> 33:50.695
Fuck, I am saying way too much.

33:52.864 --> 33:53.865
Fuck!

33:55.658 --> 33:58.202
Guards, arrest that woman. That isn't me.

34:07.628 --> 34:08.920
Shit!

35:15.947 --> 35:18.407
That's what our mother gave him
on her deathbed.

35:18.908 --> 35:21.119
Yeah, she was a lovely lady.

35:21.202 --> 35:23.371
Yeah, she was really nice to me.

35:23.454 --> 35:25.498
We had a great connection, she and I.

35:26.415 --> 35:28.251
She passed away when he was two.

35:29.377 --> 35:31.796
Right. Yeah, we talk to her sometimes.

35:33.339 --> 35:34.757
In the afterlife?

35:36.717 --> 35:37.885
Yes, she's a ghost.

35:40.805 --> 35:41.806
Okay.

35:41.889 --> 35:44.475
She... haunts.
